HST Office: VBA code can name the VBA library, and Chr gives a character on UTF-8 systems.

13% of the macro files measured write VBA.Len, VBA.Left$ or Strings.Trim: those parts name the VBA
library and its modules, and failed with "not found" or, under Option Explicit, stopped the whole module
from compiling. The names are dropped while parsing, unless the code declares or has a module of
that name.

Chr(160) or Chr(233) gave U+FFFD on Linux and macOS: one byte is no text in UTF-8. Windows-1252 is
used there; Windows keeps its ANSI code page.

